{
  "GLOBAL_PRODUCTION_BOARD_PROMPT": "Create a professional film production storyboard board for an animated short film. The entire image must resemble a real pre-production presentation board used by Pixar, DreamWorks, Disney, Netflix Animation, or AAA game cinematics. Aspect ratio 2:3 vertical. Dark charcoal blueprint background with subtle technical texture. Thin white blueprint borders. Modern production layout. Clean sans-serif typography. Perfect alignment. High-end editorial graphic design. The board must contain the following sections: [1] PROJECT HEADER including Project Title, Genre, Style, Duration, Target Platform, and Logline/Synopsis. [2] PROP REFERENCE SHEET displaying 8–12 important props, each inside an individual frame with icon and label. [3] ENVIRONMENT DESIGN SHEET displaying multiple environment thumbnails inside framed boxes. [4] COLOR PALETTE containing 8–10 official color swatches with HEX codes. [5] STORYBOARD consisting of exactly 8 numbered cinematic storyboard panels. Every storyboard panel must include scene title, timecode, action description, dialogue, camera direction, lens, movement, cinematic composition, motion arrows, camera arrows, pose indication, and transition cues exactly like a professional storyboard artist. [6] CAMERA PLAN including camera movement, shot type, camera angle, focal length, depth of field, focus behavior, framing, tracking style and lens notes. [7] LIGHTING PLAN including key light, fill light, rim light, backlight, practical lights, volumetric light, shadow direction, atmosphere, particles and color temperature. [8] ANIMATION NOTES including acting, facial expression, timing, anticipation, follow-through, squash and stretch, secondary motion, FX and particles. [9] TECHNICAL NOTES including resolution, FPS, renderer, render engine, pipeline, aspect ratio, platform, color space and output format. [10] VISUAL STYLE REFERENCES displaying six small cinematic reference images labeled Mood, Lighting, Composition, Color, Effects and Atmosphere. The overall board must look like a real animation production document prepared for pitching or production. Professional studio-quality presentation. Technical labels everywhere. Thin blueprint borders. Symmetrical modular grid layout. Small white typography. Highly organized information hierarchy. No handwritten sketches. No comic page layout. No notebook style. Looks like a genuine production board created by an experienced animation art director. Ultra-detailed. Razor sharp. Production-ready. Consistent character design. Consistent environment design. Consistent lighting. Consistent cinematic language. Premium AAA animation pre-production quality."
}
